6. Function to Show All Users:

def show_all_users():
    users = session.query(User).all()
    if users:
        for user in users:
            print(f"User {user.id}: {user.name}, {user.email}")
    else:
        print("No users found")

show_all_users():
This function queries all users in the users table and prints their information.

session.query(User).all():
Fetches all users in the users table and returns them as a list of User objects.

If there are users, it iterates through the list and prints the id, name, and email of each user.

If no users are found, it prints "No users found".


